// REJECTS: Unsupported HTTP Method type - TRACE. Supported types are - GET,POST
//
// `method: TRACE;` inside a `ServiceStore #{ ... }#` embedded-data island. The island's
// grammar takes an identifier there, so TRACE, PUT, DELETE and PATCH all lex and parse; the
// restriction to two verbs is applied while the island is being walked.
//
// Two things make this worth a fixture. First, the accepted set is SMALLER than HTTP's and
// smaller than what a reader would assume from a field called `method` -- a rewrite that
// validates against a standard HTTP verb list is more permissive on four verbs. Second, the
// message enumerates the supported set, so this fixture keeps working as documentation of
// what that set is; if upstream ever adds PUT, this line stops matching and says so.
//
// The rest of the stub is minimal but complete -- `response` is a required field of a stub
// entry, so it is supplied to keep the failure unambiguous.
###Data
Data fixture::neg::StubDataBadMethod
{
  ServiceStore
  #{
    [
      {
        request:
        {
          method: TRACE;
          url: '/employees';
        };
        response:
        {
          body: ExternalFormat #{ contentType: 'application/json'; data: '[]'; }#;
        };
      }
    ]
  }#
}
